  "notes": "Seen only on N801WA (2024-08-30, seven Commons photos the same day at Guatemala City). Everything but the body's paint is the standard scheme's, measured on N802WA; the fin and cone bands look the same in these photos. The navy wedge's edge is estimated, not fitted: the photos look down on the jet from a terminal, and the engine's shadow hides where the edge meets the belly. The aircraft isn't on World Atlantic's own fleet list (2026-11-22): it may have been repainted, stored or gone; when a newer photo turns up, check it.",
  "history": "New 2026-11-22 alongside the standard scheme. Name of this jet on the nose: 'Emily'.",
  "finish": "bareMetal"
}
